WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.250
In the world of superheroes, death is simply
a passing inconvenience.

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:08.420
If your favorite character dies a horrible
yet heroic death, well, it might sting for

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.280
a bit, but don't worry — they'll be back
sooner or later.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.820
With that in mind, here's a spoiler-filled
look at some of the superheroes we lost so

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.870
far in 2017.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.850
Rest in peace… for now.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:20.850
Logan

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.700
Wolverine has been one of the most popular
superheroes in the world for decades, thanks

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.400
in large part to Hugh Jackman, who's portrayed
the character in nine movies since the year

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.400
2000.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.160
In 2017, though, Jackman appeared in what
he swears is his final film as Wolverine,

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.120
headlining the grim Logan.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.710
Fittingly, Jackman's final appearance as Wolverine
ended with Logan's death.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:43.490
Turns out the adamantium grafted to his bones
didn't just make him indestructible — it

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:48.010
also was slowly poisoning him, pushing his
mutant healing factor beyond its capabilities.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:52.170
So when Logan faced off against an evil clone,
his battered body finally gave up the ghost

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:56.700
— but not before he heroically saved a group
of mutant kids, including a totally different,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.970
totally not evil little girl clone.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:02.670
So at least some of Logan lives on somewhere,
even if it might be a little too confusing

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.390
to understand.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:05.880
Professor Charles Xavier

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:10.050
Dedicated to the proposition that all men
are created equal, Professor Xavier has been

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.740
pursuing his dream since 1963.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:16.500
And for the better part of two decades, Patrick
Stewart has been one of a pair of actors portraying

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.510
the good professor on the big screen.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:21.920
Sadly, the Professor's dream turned into a
nightmare in the film Logan.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.860
After suffering a seizure that accidentally
caused him to kill all his own students, Xavier

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.640
was put into a drugged stupor by his last
remaining pupil, Logan.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.150
Professor X's pain finally came to an end
when Logan's evil clone killed him right in

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.520
the middle of a road trip to the woods of
North Dakota.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.590
That seems like a fittingly convoluted way
for the original X-Man to die.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:40.790
Jack Flag

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:44.740
First debuting back in 1994, Jack Harrison
was originally a member of a citizen's patrol

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.300
group who responded to reports submitted to
Captain America's danger hotline.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.280
But during a fight with Mr. Hyde, he got drenched
in super chemicals and became a real deal

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.950
superpowered hero under the name Jack Flag.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:58.600
After bouncing around the Marvel Universe
for two decades, even joining the Guardians

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.420
of the Galaxy at one point, Jack Flag and
his on-again-off-again partner Free Spirit

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.260
were eventually recruited by Captain America
to Join SHIELD.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:08.950
Unknown to them, however, Steve had been turned
evil by the reality-warping powers of the

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:11.450
Cosmic Cube and was actually working for Hydra.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:15.220
Jack discovered this the hard way when Steve
Rogers tossed him out of a plane.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:18.950
Jack survived the fall, but was left brain
dead until Free Spirit decided to pull the

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:19.950
plug.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.400
Jack, we hoist a patriotic face bandana to
your memory.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.400
Hack

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.630
When you join a team called the Suicide Squad,
you have to know your time is limited.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:31.099
The superhero known as Hack found this out
the hard way.

00:02:31.099 --> 00:02:35.319
A tech-savvy metahuman who grew up in the
slums of Nairobi, Hack had the unique ability

00:02:35.319 --> 00:02:39.110
to interact with computers using her mind,
allowing her to surf the web and download

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:43.280
information directly into her head, as well
as turn people into digital code and transport

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.450
them through the internet.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:48.760
But rather than simply use her powers to binge-watch
YouTube, Hack decided to help the Suicide

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:49.760
Squad.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:53.210
Along the way, she accidentally discovered
that the team had traitors in their midst.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:57.110
Before she could reveal this shocking information,
one of those traitors, Captain Boomerang,

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.290
stabbed her to death.

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.150
Alas, poor Hack.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.060
We hardly knew ye.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.060
Patriot

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.860
When it comes to classic superheroes, it doesn't
get much more old school than Jeffrey Mace,

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:09.060
The Patriot, who first debuted way back in
1941.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.440
Though his heyday in the comics ended long
ago, The Patriot got a second lease on life

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.319
thanks to Marvel's Agents of SHIELD, where
he appeared in season four as the spy agency's

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:18.319
new director.

00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:22.080
Blessed with powers thanks to a super soldier
serum, Mace ended up entering the virtual

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.870
reality program called The Framework in order
to rescue some of his agents.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:30.560
And just like in The Matrix, if you die in
the Framework, you die in reality too.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.900
"Whoa."

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:36.269
While Mace performed a rescue inside the program,
Madame Hydra blew up the building he was in.

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:39.709
Mace was able to use his powers to save everyone
else in the building and give them time to

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:42.920
escape — but at the cost of his own life.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:46.460
"Coulsen?" "I'm right here, hang on."

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.320
"Go."

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.240
Bucky Barnes, The Winter soldier

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:54.440
That used to be one basic rule when it came
to bringing back dead characters: everyone

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:59.400
could return except for Peter Parker's Uncle
Ben and Captain Amercia's sidekick Bucky Barnes,

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.980
who died while trying to defuse one of Baron
Zemo's flying bombs during World War II.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:07.540
That rule was famously violated, though, when
Bucky returned from the dead as the Soviet

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.970
sleeper super agent, the Winter Soldier.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:14.250
However, all good things must come to an end,
including Bucky's second life.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:18.239
After Captain America was turned evil by the
Cosmic Cube, evil Steve Rogers teamed up with

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:19.379
the new Baron Zemo.

00:04:19.379 --> 00:04:23.539
They captured Bucky, and, in a cruel twist,
re-enacted his original death by strapping

00:04:23.539 --> 00:04:27.409
him to a replica of that same flying bomb
and blowing him sky high.

00:04:27.409 --> 00:04:29.710
Don't worry, though, he'll probably be back.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:32.060
After all, it's happened before.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:33.060
"Bucky?"

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:35.090
"Who the hell is Bucky?"

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:36.090
Thanks for watching!

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:38.099
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:38.099 --> 00:04:40.470
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

